Manage all git repositories (public & private) with $HOME as work tree.

  lpex mgit <public|private|all> <action> [repo] …

  list   [repo] [--files]          repositories, remotes, tracked paths
  status [repo]                    changes + files the next push adds
  add    <repo> <path>             track a file/directory (safety checks)
  rm     <repo> <path>             stop tracking (files stay on disk)
  push   [repo] [--message …]      pick up new files, commit, upload
  pull   [repo]                    update; clones repositories missing here
  create <repo> [--path <dir>]     new repository on the servers + locally
  import <repo> [--path <dir>]     take over an existing server repository with history
  delete <repo> [--local-only]     delete on the servers + locally (asks for the name)
  git    <repo> <git-args…>        raw git with git-dir/work-tree set
  check  <repo>                    (public) secret check, used as pre-commit hook
  apply  [--collect]               (private) install root-owned files, e.g. sudoers

'all' offers list, status, push and pull over both areas.
Without --path a repository is a home repository (work tree $HOME, tracked roots);
with --path it is a project repository (own folder, whole folder tracked, own .gitignore).
Branch = area name (public | private); import keeps the server's branch. Servers: lpex --config mgit
Data: ~/.local/state/lpex/data/mgit/ (git dirs in repos/ are never tracked)
